- tests/smoke/test_e2e_flows.py::TestQwenProfilesE2E and
  ::TestQwenRecoveryE2E assert controller state, QML surface state (profile
  combo/badge, voice picker rows, generate enablement + disabled reason,
  Studio clip provenance labels and the mismatch banner), the artifact (48 kHz,
  24 000 samples), the on-disk clone store, and the frames each host RECEIVED
  (load/synthesize/cancel/shutdown per build) plus host liveness at every step.
- src/vienetts_app/core/qwen_engine.py: `_write_frame_safely` guards the
  parent→host write. The app restores SIGPIPE's default disposition when its
  own stdout is a pipe (`_restore_default_sigpipe`), so the cleanup frame
  written after a host died mid-job killed the whole process (observed as exit
  -13 under pytest, where stdout is a pipe). The guard blocks SIGPIPE for the
  writing thread, consumes the signal a failed write raises, and lets the
  caller surface the actionable QwenEngineError instead. Verified by
  tests/unit/test_qwen_engine.py::TestInferStream::
  test_a_dead_host_pipe_never_kills_the_process (fails as a process kill
  without the fix, passes with it), which sets SIG_DFL explicitly so it holds
  regardless of how pytest was launched.
- tests/smoke/test_ui_tabs.py needed no change: the Qwen install cards,
  profile/language controls, cloning capability notice and the Studio mismatch
  banner are already asserted there at the stub level (Tasks 6.1–6.4); this
  task adds the consolidated real-stack scenarios the plan asks for.

